course: dictionary
lesson: 10689
title: Unreal: not real, amazing or unfair?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The start of unreal is un-, which often means not. So unreal means not real. Real things are true and you can touch them. Unreal things are imaginary, like a dream or a made-up world.
explain: Unreal can also describe something so shocking that it is hard to believe. «It felt unreal» when big news arrived. The clue is the feeling: the news was so big it seemed impossible, not fake.
explain: In slang, unreal can mean amazing. «That goal was unreal!» The speaker is not saying the goal did not happen. The excitement tells you it means brilliant. Other slang can mean unfair: «The price is unreal» means it is ridiculous and far too high. Ask yourself: is the speaker excited or annoyed?
fact: Unreal means not real, imaginary or like a dream.
fact: «It felt unreal» can mean something is so shocking that it is hard to believe.
fact: In slang, «unreal» means amazing or brilliant, as in «That goal was unreal!»
fact: In slang, «unreal» can also mean unfair or ridiculous, as in «The price is unreal.»
fact: «Delulu» is young slang for believing something unreal.
exercise: «The dragon in the story was unreal, a creature from a dream.» What does unreal mean here? | Hungry and tired | Real and heavy | Wet and grey | *Not real, imaginary
exercise: «That goal was unreal!» What does unreal mean in this slang? | *Amazing or brilliant | Dull and boring | Not real, so the goal did not happen | Unfair and too high
exercise: Priya says, «The price is unreal.» What does she mean? | Brilliant and cheap | Imaginary, like a dream | *Ridiculous, far too high and unfair | Sad and small
test: «It felt unreal when the news came through.» What does unreal suggest? | Very wet and grey | *So shocking it was hard to believe | Easy to understand | Made of wood
test: Kai says, «You're delulu if you think you'll win.» What does delulu mean? | Telling the truth | Winning every game | *Believing something unreal | Running very fast
exam: Lily says, «That goal was unreal!» What does she mean? | Unfair and ridiculous | Dull and boring | Not real, the goal never happened | *Brilliant
